 '<i>Brahma-saṃsparśa</i>, “contact with Brahman”, is a striking phrase. The sense pleasures of 5.22 were <i>saṃsparśa-ja</i>, born of contact, and full of sorrow; this contact is with the infinite, and full of joy. Commentators note the contrast. <i>Sukhena</i>, easily, is encouraging: what began as effort becomes natural. Śaṅkara says the yogi enjoys the bliss of Brahman effortlessly. Rāmānuja says the yogi easily enjoys the bliss of the self. The meditation section, 6.10–28, ends here; the next verses describe the vision that follows.',
