 'This is Arjuna’s fifth question, and his most relatable. Commentators praise his honesty. After hearing the beautiful descriptions of 6.10–32, he says: I don’t see how this can last, because my mind is restless. Many readers feel he speaks for them. The name <i>Madhusūdana</i>, slayer of the demon Madhu, may hint: you killed a demon; can you kill this one? Śaṅkara notes that Arjuna’s doubt is about the stability of the state, not its value. Kṛṣṇa’s answer (6.35–36) does not dismiss the problem.',
