DEEP[34]=('',
 'Arjuna gives four words for the mind. <i>Cañcala</i>, flickering, restless. <i>Pramāthin</i>, churning, agitating (the same word used of the senses in 2.60). <i>Balavat</i>, strong. <i>Dṛḍha</i>, tough, stubborn. Commentators note that he calls Kṛṣṇa by name here, a sign of earnestness. The wind image is apt: one cannot grasp the wind in a fist. The Kaṭha Upaniṣad (1.3.4–6) compares the senses to horses and the mind to reins. Arjuna feels the reins slipping. Kṛṣṇa does not argue; he agrees and gives a method.',
 'Describe your mind honestly: restless? stubborn? anxious? Naming its habits is the first step to working with them.')
