 'Kṛṣṇa begins by agreeing: <i>asaṃśayam</i>, no doubt about it. Commentators admire the teaching style. Patañjali’s Yoga Sūtra (1.12) gives the same two keys: <i>abhyāsa-vairāgyābhyāṃ tan-nirodhaḥ</i>, “the stilling is by practice and detachment”. <i>Abhyāsa</i> is repeated effort over a long time (Yoga Sūtra 1.14 says it must be long, unbroken and devoted). <i>Vairāgya</i> is loosening the pull of desire. Śaṅkara says practice is returning the mind again and again to one object; detachment is seeing the faults of other objects. Together they work.',
