 '<i>Upāya</i>, right means or method, is the key word. Commentators note that effort without method can be wasted; method without effort is empty. Śaṅkara says the means are the practice and detachment just described. Rāmānuja says the means include karma yoga, which purifies the mind. Kṛṣṇa does not promise ease. He says <i>śakya</i>, possible. That honesty is reassuring: the difficulty is real, and so is the possibility.',
